<title>GERMANY: TRINKAUS SAYS H1 OPER PROFIT UP 10 PCT.</title>
<headline>TRINKAUS SAYS H1 OPER PROFIT UP 10 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    85.3   vs 77.6</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		     14.1   vs 18.0</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 127.3  vs 125.0</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     122.7  vs 96.1</p>
<p>    Group administration costs		162.7  vs 149.7</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 19,319 vs 18,678</p>
<p>    Grou business volume			21,209 vs 20,590</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Trinkaus &amp; Burkhardt KGaA, a subsidiary of HSBC Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
